From bf9e0b90f4a4908f3e24b9bd28648a9ab1955a9c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 21:26:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Build the game for the PS Vita (THPS_ARCH=vita):
 toolchain, runtime, VPK

arm-vita-eabi from VITASDK: game code and data with -fno-short-enums (ARM EABI's
1-byte enums broke CBruce's layout) and -fpcc-struct-return (egcs/MIPS aggregate
returns), the runtime's Vita platform layer (ux0:data/THPS, a synced log, env.txt
for the environment, no fault handlers), the R3000's division-by-zero results
through wrapped EABI division helpers, and thps.vpk packaging. The renderer is
still the OpenGL 3.3 one. psyq_sigmatch.py takes PSYQ_SIGDIR.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NwhU758snL1NnmSbmmwENz
